WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.262 --> 00:00:06.930
I’m in trouble, Mr. Potter.

00:00:07.723 --> 00:00:08.974
I need help.

00:00:10.017 --> 00:00:11.351
Look at you.

00:00:11.351 --> 00:00:13.520
You used to be so cocky.

00:00:13.520 --> 00:00:16.606
You were going to go out and conquer
the world.

00:00:16.606 --> 00:00:21.194
You once called me a warped,
frustrated old man.

00:00:22.154 --> 00:00:23.530
What are you but a warped, 

00:00:23.530 --> 00:00:25.490
frustrated, young man.

00:00:31.538 --> 00:00:33.707
Miserable little clerk crawling in

00:00:33.707 --> 00:00:36.710
here on your hands and knees
and begging for help.

00:00:39.588 --> 00:00:40.630
Dog gonnit.

00:00:41.256 --> 00:00:43.884
You sit around here
and you spin your little webs,

00:00:43.884 --> 00:00:46.136
and you think the whole world
revolves around you and your money.

00:00:46.136 --> 00:00:48.055
Well, it doesn’t, Mr. Potter.

00:00:48.055 --> 00:00:49.806
And that goes for you, too.

00:00:54.227 --> 00:00:56.438
And it goes for you, too.

00:01:03.945 --> 00:01:04.821
Ernie, take me home.

00:01:04.821 --> 00:01:06.448
I’m going off my nut.

00:01:06.448 --> 00:01:09.534
Civil defense authorities
have told newsmen that murder victims

00:01:09.785 --> 00:01:13.288
show evidence of having been
partially devoured by their murderers.

00:01:13.497 --> 00:01:17.125
Medical examination of victims
bodies shows conclusively that the killers

00:01:17.125 --> 00:01:19.920
are eating the flesh of the people
they killed.

00:01:20.337 --> 00:01:21.463
Okay, well just step on.

00:01:21.463 --> 00:01:22.339
Just get me home.

00:01:22.339 --> 00:01:24.466
It would appear that
no one is safe from this wave—

00:01:34.184 --> 00:01:35.268
Hello, darling.

00:01:43.735 --> 00:01:45.946
Must she keep playing that?

00:01:45.946 --> 00:01:48.573
I have to practice it
for the party tonight, Daddy.

00:01:49.866 --> 00:01:51.326
What’s the matter with Zuzu?

00:01:51.326 --> 00:01:53.537
She’s got a cold. She’s in bed.

00:01:53.537 --> 00:01:55.497
One of those things grabbed her.

00:01:55.497 --> 00:01:56.706
Bit her on the arm.

00:01:56.706 --> 00:01:57.958
Is she running a temperature?

00:01:57.958 --> 00:01:58.417
What is it?

00:01:58.417 --> 00:02:01.420
Just a teensy one, 99.6.
She’ll be alright.

00:02:02.087 --> 00:02:03.296
Isn’t it 3:00 yet?

00:02:03.296 --> 00:02:05.298
How should I know?
What do you think I am, a dictionary?

00:02:05.298 --> 00:02:06.800
Tommy! Stop that! Stop it!

00:02:06.800 --> 00:02:08.635
Janie, haven’t you learned 
that silly tune yet?

00:02:08.635 --> 00:02:11.096
You play it over and over again.
Now stop it, stop it!

00:02:11.096 --> 00:02:12.848
Oh, Daddy.

00:02:32.284 --> 00:02:32.993
Oh, hello Nick.

00:02:32.993 --> 00:02:34.870
Hey, where’s Martini?

00:02:34.870 --> 00:02:37.330
You want a martini?
Oh, no. Martini, your boss.

00:02:37.330 --> 00:02:37.998
Where is he?

00:02:37.998 --> 00:02:40.459
Hey, look, I’m the boss. 
You want a drink or don’t you?

00:02:40.459 --> 00:02:43.128
Ok, alright. Double bourbon, 
will you? Quick, huh?

00:02:44.379 --> 00:02:46.256
It’s hot in here.

00:02:46.256 --> 00:02:47.174
Hot.

00:02:47.174 --> 00:02:50.635
We serve hard drinks in here for men
who want to get drunk fast.

00:02:50.635 --> 00:02:54.306
And we don’t need any characters around
to give the joint atmosphere.

00:02:54.306 --> 00:02:55.432
Is that clear?

00:02:55.432 --> 00:02:58.977
We came to put a wreath
on my father’s grave,

00:03:00.187 --> 00:03:03.398
and then this man started 
walking up the road.

00:03:04.107 --> 00:03:05.901
He came slowly, 

00:03:05.901 --> 00:03:08.403
and Johnny kept teasing me 
and saying

00:03:08.403 --> 00:03:10.822
He’s coming to get you,
Barbara.

00:03:11.823 --> 00:03:14.784
And I laughed at him and said,
Johnny, stop it.

00:03:14.784 --> 00:03:18.038
And then Johnny ran away, and I—

00:03:18.997 --> 00:03:22.250
I went up to this man and he grabbed me.

00:03:23.793 --> 00:03:25.879
He grabbed me

00:03:25.879 --> 00:03:28.548
and he ripped at me.

00:03:28.548 --> 00:03:29.925
That does it.

00:03:29.925 --> 00:03:32.469
Out you two pixies go through the door

00:03:32.469 --> 00:03:33.512
or out the window.

00:03:36.723 --> 00:03:37.599
Stay out.

00:03:41.019 --> 00:03:42.896
Hey, what’s going on around here?

00:04:25.855 --> 00:04:28.275
This is the latest disclosure 
in a report from

00:04:28.275 --> 00:04:30.443
National Civil Defense headquarters 
in Washington.

00:04:30.652 --> 00:04:31.820
Gotta fix these boards.

00:04:31.820 --> 00:04:34.823
It has been established
that persons who have recently died

00:04:35.365 --> 00:04:38.952
have been returning to life
and committing acts of murder.

00:04:40.078 --> 00:04:42.956
All law enforcement agencies
and the military

00:04:42.956 --> 00:04:46.459
have been organized to search out
and destroy the marauding ghouls.

00:04:46.459 --> 00:04:50.338
The Survival Command Center
at the Pentagon has disclosed that

00:04:50.338 --> 00:04:54.050
a ghoul can be killed
by a shot in the head,

00:04:54.467 --> 00:04:57.470
or a heavy blow to the skull.

00:04:58.305 --> 00:05:01.308
I wonder what Martini put in those drinks.

00:05:38.511 --> 00:05:39.888
Yeah!

00:05:43.975 --> 00:05:45.143
Merry Christmas.

00:05:45.435 --> 00:05:47.145
Merry Christmas.

00:05:47.562 --> 00:05:48.855
Merry Christmas.

00:05:49.564 --> 00:05:51.024
Mary?

00:05:51.024 --> 00:05:53.985
Merry Christmas, Daddy.

00:05:53.985 --> 00:05:54.986
Kids!

00:05:56.321 --> 00:05:57.739
Kids! Janie!

00:05:57.739 --> 00:05:59.324
Tommy!

00:05:59.324 --> 00:06:00.200
Daddy!

00:06:00.200 --> 00:06:02.952
Zuzu! Zuzu, my little ginger snap.

00:06:02.952 --> 00:06:03.870
How do you feel? 

00:06:03.870 --> 00:06:04.579
Fine.

00:06:04.579 --> 00:06:05.747
Not a smidge of temperature.

00:06:05.747 --> 00:06:08.792
Not a smidge of— Hallelujah.

00:06:09.000 --> 00:06:09.500
Hello.

00:06:10.502 --> 00:06:11.461
George.

00:06:11.461 --> 00:06:15.215
George, darling, where have you—
Oh, George.

00:06:15.298 --> 00:06:16.132
George.

00:06:16.132 --> 00:06:17.926
You have no idea what’s happened to me.

00:06:17.926 --> 00:06:19.678
Oh, come on, George, come on downstairs.

00:06:19.678 --> 00:06:20.720
Quick! They’re on their way!

00:06:20.720 --> 00:06:21.262
All right.

00:06:21.262 --> 00:06:22.722
Come on.

00:06:24.766 --> 00:06:26.226
Come on in here now.

00:06:26.685 --> 00:06:27.936
It’s a miracle.

00:06:29.813 --> 00:06:31.272
Who’s gonna come, Daddy?

00:06:31.981 --> 00:06:33.441
Come in, Uncle Billy.

00:06:33.441 --> 00:06:35.485
Everybody in here!

00:06:35.485 --> 00:06:36.444
George.

00:06:36.736 --> 00:06:38.321
George!

00:06:38.321 --> 00:06:40.573
I’ve never seen anything like it.

00:06:47.622 --> 00:06:50.041
I made the rounds of my charge accounts.

00:06:53.503 --> 00:06:54.838
There you are, George.

00:06:54.838 --> 00:06:57.048
I got the faculty all up out of bed.

00:06:57.048 --> 00:06:58.800
And here’s something for 
you to play with.

00:07:01.219 --> 00:07:02.220
Mr. Martini,

00:07:02.220 --> 00:07:03.513
how about some wine?

00:07:19.562 --> 00:07:21.656
No, no!

00:07:21.656 --> 00:07:23.950
Johnny, no! 

00:07:24.451 --> 00:07:26.453
No, no!

00:07:27.162 --> 00:07:30.165
Help me, help me, help—

